## 🚦 CHAPTER 13: Common Errors and What They Mean

| Error | Meaning | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `insmod: ERROR: could not insert module chardev.ko: Invalid module format` | Module compiled for different kernel version | Rebuild: `make clean && make all` |
| `insmod: ERROR: could not insert module chardev.ko: Operation not permitted` | Not running as root | Use `sudo insmod` |
| `open: No such file or directory` | `/dev/chardev` doesn't exist | Check `dmesg` — did `device_create` fail? |
| `open: Device or resource busy` | Mutex held — another process has it open | Close the other process first |
| Kernel panic | Bug in your driver code | Restore VM snapshot, fix the bug |
| `make: Nothing to be done` | No changes since last build | Touch the file: `touch chardev.c && make` |

